# An instruction the classifier does not model inside a counted loop:
# the loop's flop and global/shared byte totals carry `+ unknown`, the
# flops' per-precision entries do not (they are what was counted), and
# AI(global) has no direction because both sides are lower bounds.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/unknown_in_loop.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
CHECK: kernel micro_unknown_in_loop
CHECK: trips = param_1
CHECK: wgmma.fence.sync.aligned  1
CHECK: flops = 2 + unknown  (f32 2)
CHECK: tensor flops = 0 + unknown
CHECK: global bytes: load 4 B + unknown, store 4 B + unknown
CHECK: AI(global): not bounded (flops are a lower bound, global bytes are a lower bound)
CHECK: unknowns:
CHECK: instruction `wgmma` x1 — not classified — its flops/bytes are not counted
